# YADS — line-ending policy.
#
# The whole repository is LF in the index AND in the working tree. This is not
# taste: `make_art.py` writes every generated .meta.toml / .toml / .json with
# newline="\n" (make_art.py:1590), so any CRLF in the tree would make the
# generator's own "a clean run is byte-identical" contract false on Windows,
# and a `git diff` of a mod file would render as a whole-file rewrite instead of
# the two lines that actually moved. Beta 1.0's rename audit lost real signal to
# exactly that.
#
# `eol=lf` (rather than bare `text`) pins the WORKING TREE too, so core.autocrlf
# on a contributor's Windows box cannot check the files back out as CRLF.

*               text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the file kinds this repo actually contains.
*.gml           text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.bbcode        text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf

# Never touched, never diffed as text. The sprites and the contact sheet are
# generator output; a normalization pass over them would corrupt them.
*.png           binary
*.zip           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary
*.wav           binary
*.ogg           binary
